//? Title: PCNN: actual synchronous pulse dynamics
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This native simplified model uses each pixel stimulus times one plus beta times
its previous eight-neighbor pulse sum. It decays the threshold, tests strict
activity>threshold, then adds the refractory gain after firing. All pixels read
only previous pulses; row order does not propagate same-iteration firing.
Initial threshold need not exceed the image maximum. Brightness ordering and
synchronization are fixture-dependent observations, not a segmentation-quality
guarantee. The synthetic original disk isolates intensity and local coupling, so
no empirical dataset is introduced.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

This native simplified model uses each pixel stimulus times one plus beta times
its previous eight-neighbor pulse sum. It decays the threshold, tests strict
activity>threshold, then adds the refractory gain after firing. All pixels read
only previous pulses; row order does not propagate same-iteration firing.
Initial threshold need not exceed the image maximum. Brightness ordering and
synchronization are fixture-dependent observations, not a segmentation-quality
guarantee. The synthetic original disk isolates intensity and local coupling, so
no empirical dataset is introduced.

$$ L_{ij}^{(n)}=\sum_{(u,v)\in N_8(i,j)}Y_{uv}^{(n-1)},\quad U_{ij}^{(n)}=S_{ij}(1+\beta L_{ij}^{(n)}),\quad Y_{ij}^{(n)}=1[U_{ij}^{(n)}>\alpha\Theta_{ij}^{(n-1)}]. $$

After that strict comparison, the threshold becomes alpha times the old
threshold plus gain times the actual pulse. The stronger-coupling control uses
beta2 explicitly; the original disk retains beta0.2.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pcnn_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::PCNNParameters p;
    p.iterations = 2;
    auto t = dm::algorithms::pcnn_trace({{.9, .3}}, p);
    std::print("| iteration | column | previous neighbor sum | activity | decayed threshold | pulse | after " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.cells)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.iteration,
                   r.column, r.linking, r.activity, r.decayed, r.pulse, r.after);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual cell updates\n{}", t.cells.size()));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual firing counts\n{}", t.result.time_signature));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual first-fire times\n{}", t.result.first_fire[0]));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pcnn_tiny.svg");
}
```
